# Text is stored and checked out with LF on every platform. Git for Windows defaults to
# converting text to CRLF on checkout, and both format gates read bytes: `gofmt -l` lists
# every Go file with CRLF endings and `prettier --check` rejects every web file, so the
# Windows leg of the CI matrix could not pass on a default checkout. The release archives
# are built from an LF tree; this keeps a Windows checkout identical to what is shipped.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.docx binary
